Always be concise. No conversational filler. Use pytest for math logic. Keep code modular. Prioritize performance.

# Team Protocol

Specialist roles (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`):

- backend — numerical stability, vectorization, math tests
- frontend — Streamlit UI, DataFrame inputs, `st.cache_data`, dark-mode layout
- github — sync, atomic commits, conflict reporting
- audit — read-only completeness / `product_spec.md` compliance; flag Integration Gaps
- compliance — API security, `.gitignore` integrity, secrets management
- perf — vectorization, `st.cache_data` optimization, memory profiling
- qa — pytest generation, mathematical boundary testing
- ux — docstrings, tooltips, user-friendly labels
- quant — Quant Strategist: statistical edge, PoP/Monte Carlo, Greek-neutral hedges

Institutional Tier readiness: compliance, perf, qa, and ux required alongside core roles.

Protocol: Before the Architect approves any new trading feature, the Quant Strategist must perform a Statistical Sanity Check — ensure the logic is not directional betting, but a mathematical edge.
